 "notes": [
  "Story URLs look like {section}.slashdot.org/story/YY/MM/DD/ID/slug. get-story and list-story-comments take yy/mm/dd/id, and slashdot.org redirects to the right section subdomain. Keep leading zeros in id.",
  "fetch-all-comments needs the numeric discussion id (sid), not the story path id. The sid appears in comment links (comments.pl?sid=...).",
  "Keyword search (search.pl), single comment pages (comments.pl?cid=..., behind a Cloudflare bot check), /submission/<id> pages and ?issue=YYYYMMDD day pages are blocked or disallowed. Use list-by-tag (fhfilter) as the closest thing to search.",
  "list-user-comments returns alternating rows: comment rows have subject/url/date, and 'attached to' rows name the parent story.",
  "archive.pl?op=topics or ?op=sections without a keyword returns the list of available topics/sections instead of stories.",
  "vote-poll is a real write. Slashdot allows only one vote per IP per poll.",
  "Everything was explored anonymously, and no command needs login."
 ],
